  "notes": "COMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {食欲|しょくよく}をそそる: to whet one's appetite (the most common usage)\n- {好奇心|こうきしん}をそそる: to arouse curiosity\n- {興味|きょうみ}をそそる: to pique interest\n\nUSAGE: Most commonly encountered in the set phrase {食欲|しょくよく}をそそる. The subject is typically the thing that stimulates (a smell, a sight), and the object is the feeling being aroused.",
